// Server environment overrides for the YOLO bridge.
// Copy to server/.env for machine-specific paths, or just set them as real
// environment variables before `npm run dev:all`.
//
// ── DATABASE (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Leave DATABASE_URL unset and NEXORA runs on the JSON files in server/data/,
// exactly as it did before. That fallback is permanent, not a stopgap: if the
// database is down or unreachable the app keeps serving from JSON, and
// GET /api/health reports which backend is live under "db".
//
//   $env:DATABASE_URL = "postgresql://nexora:nexora@localhost:5432/nexora"
//
// Then apply the schema and load the existing data once:
//   node scripts/migrate.mjs
//   node scripts/migrate.mjs --verify     # compare row counts, writes nothing
//
// See server/DATABASE_SETUP.md for the full walkthrough.
// DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nexora:nexora@localhost:5432/nexora
// PG_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
// PG_POOL_MAX=10
//
// ── YOLO weight files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Leave these unset to use the default locations:
//     server/models/fire_smoke.pt
//     server/models/flood.pt
// Point them at your weights only if you keep the .pt files elsewhere.
//
// YOLO_MODEL_FIRE_SMOKE=D:\sutharson\yolo\fire and smoke\best.pt
// YOLO_MODEL_FLOOD=D:\sutharson\yolo\flood\best.pt
//
// ── COCO context pass (person / car) ──────────────────────────────────────────
// A third, optional detector. The bundled weights cannot see people or cars
// (fire_smoke.pt is {fire, smoke}; flood.pt is {Flooding, Potholes, Waste
// Management}), so this runs a COCO-pretrained model to add real person/car/
// boat boxes as situational awareness. Those boxes NEVER change the disaster
// verdict. Default weights: yolo11n.pt, downloaded once on first run (~5.4 MB).
//
// YOLO_MODEL_CONTEXT=D:\weights\yolo11n.pt
// YOLO_CONTEXT_CONF=0.30   # stricter than the disaster models: COCO is trained
//                          # on everyday photos and floods the panel with junk
//                          # (debris, roof tiles, reflections) at 0.15
// YOLO_CONTEXT_IMGSZ=960
//
// ── Python interpreter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Defaults to `python` on PATH. Set this if the wrong one is picked up, e.g.
// when the Microsoft Store python.exe alias shadows your real install.
// YOLO_PYTHON=C:\Users\Admin1\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python312\python.exe
//
// ── Inference timeout (ms, default 120000) ───────────────────────────────────
// YOLO_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
//
// ── Inference tuning (recall-optimised — see YOLO_SETUP.md) ─────────────────
// YOLO_CONF=0.15      # was 0.25; lower catches faint smoke / thin floodwater
// YOLO_IMGSZ=960      # was 640; needed for small & distant fire sources
// YOLO_IOU=0.7        # stops NMS merging adjacent fire zones
// YOLO_MAX_DET=300    // ceiling for dense scenes
// YOLO_AUGMENT=1      // test-time augmentation — biggest single win
